WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Language2Drive asks whether driving models follow language across two feasible alternatives.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A Paired Counterfactual Unit keeps the scene, seed and initial state fixed.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Run the same model independently. Change only the mutually exclusive instruction.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Both alternatives must satisfy their execution requirements for strict paired success.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Select the requested turn, lane change or parking maneuver.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Maintain a speed, lane or following constraint over time.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Connect words to locations and objects in the observed scene.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Remember the goal and execute the required stages in order.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Model result: CARLA execution replay under paired lane instructions.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Conditional destinations bring scene understanding and multi-stage instructions into the same evaluation.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Model result: Alpamayo 1.5 in reconstructed RealSim driving scenes.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Compare instruction-conditioned model forecasts in the same recorded camera context.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Switch models on the same paired case to inspect their responses to the requested speed.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Benchmark targets: NAVSIM reference trajectories define the two requested outcomes.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Compare instruction-conditioned model predictions on a shared coordinate scale.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
WOD-E2E benchmark targets illustrate two requested behaviors in the same observed scene.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Paired speed requirements define the requested outcomes over shared real-world camera context.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Adapt once, configure the resources, and run the native evaluations across three runtime groups.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Evaluate your model. Share native scores, execution coverage and reproducible evidence.
